  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "The landing page presents OncoReady as a finished buyer-oriented SaaS business solution and contains no demo, prototype, preview, portfolio, or training framing.",
    "The patient, staff, and caregiver cards under 'Built around everyone responsible for tomorrow.' reveal once on viewport entry using distinct but coherent, non-blocking variants with no layout shift.",
    "The former Deployment paths area becomes a SaaS business-model section explaining the institutional buyer, subscribed treatment-readiness capability, configuration or implementation shape, and expansion path.",
    "Scrolling through the production landing build and every workspace has no repeatable section-boundary pause, horizontal overflow, or nested-scroll trap; reveal effects add no continuous scroll listener or render loop.",
    "System or in-product reduced motion renders all reveal content immediately, disables smooth entrance behavior, and preserves equivalent content, focus, status, and route behavior.",
    "Landing, sign-in, patient, all staff destinations, caregiver, system, modals, shared navigation, and mobile dock use a coherent Clinical Glass visual language while preserving operational hierarchy and meaningful states.",
    "The caregiver surface remains transportation-only and exposes no clinical concern or nurse-only detail after the visual refresh.",
    "The complete landing-to-confirmed-plan Maria journey, workspace navigation, reset, persistence, search and filtering, FAQ, map fallback, and responsive layouts continue to work.",
    "The production build, existing critical-path checks, focused reveal/reduced-motion/copy checks, and independent targeted test report pass on the integrated revision."
  ],
